---
import { u } from '../lib/url';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import { contactEmail, legal } from '../data/site';
const email = contactEmail;
---
<Base title="Privacy policy" description="How Shiva Swarodaya, run by The Shakti Multiversity, collects, uses and protects personal information.">
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy policy" lede={`Last updated: ${legal.lastUpdated}`} />

  <article class="article">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container prose legal-text">
        <p class="summary">In short: we collect only what we need to teach you and to answer you. Your details are kept in our own student register, our email service receives only your first name and email address, nothing is sold, and you can ask us to see, correct or delete your information at any time.</p>

        <h2 id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>shivaswarodaya.com (“Shiva Swarodaya”, “we”, “us”) is run by <strong>{legal.operator}</strong>, {legal.address}. We decide why and how your personal information is used, which makes us the <em>data fiduciary</em> under India’s Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.</p>
        <p>For anything in this policy, write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>

        <h2 id="what">2. What we collect, and why</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="What we collect, and why">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">When</th><th scope="col">What</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">You register for a course</th><td>First name, email address and country. Your WhatsApp number and your experience of yoga, if you give them. The date and the wording of the consent you gave.</td><td>To send the welcome email and the daily lessons; to keep a record of who is studying; to understand who is joining so the teaching can be pitched well; to contact you about the course on WhatsApp if you gave your number.</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">You agree to news</th><td>Your email address and first name.</td><td>To tell you, a few times a year, about new courses, weekly sessions and the annual retreat.</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">You write to us</th><td>Your name, email address, the topic and your message.</td><td>To reply to you.</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">You visit the site</th><td>Technical information recorded by our web host, such as your IP address, browser type and the pages requested.</td><td>To keep the site working and secure. We do not use it to identify you.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>We do not ask for sensitive information such as health details, and we do not take payments on this site. If paid courses are offered later, payments will be handled by a payment provider under its own privacy policy, and this page will be updated first.</p>
        <p>We do not use your information for advertising, we do not sell or rent it, and we do not make automated decisions about you.</p>

        <h2 id="consent">3. Your consent</h2>
        <p>We use your personal information on the basis of your consent: the box you tick when you register, or the message you choose to send us. You can withdraw consent at any time, as easily as you gave it, by using the unsubscribe link at the foot of every email or by writing to us. Withdrawing consent stops future use; it does not affect what was done before.</p>

        <h2 id="where">4. Where your information is kept</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Our student register</strong> is a Google Sheet in our own Google account. Google stores it on its servers, which may be in India or elsewhere.</li>
          <li><strong>Our email service, Brevo</strong> (a French company), receives only your first name and email address, in order to send the course emails and news. Brevo stores data in the European Union.</li>
          <li><strong>Our web host</strong> (currently GitHub, Inc., USA) records basic technical information about visits to keep the site running.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These services act on our instructions and are not allowed to use your information for their own purposes. Some of them store data outside India, as Indian law permits.</p>

        <h2 id="others">5. Other services on the site</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>YouTube.</strong> Our videos are on YouTube. When you follow a link to a video, or play one, YouTube’s own privacy policy applies.</li>
          <li><strong>Calendar.</strong> The weekly sessions on the Calendar are read from a public Google Sheet when you open that page. No information about you is sent with that request beyond what any web request carries.</li>
          <li><strong>Fonts</strong> are served from this site itself, not from Google.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics.</strong> The site does not use analytics at present. If we add a service such as Google Analytics, it will be switched on only after you agree to it, and this policy will be updated first.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="cookies">6. Cookies</h2>
        <p>The site does not set cookies. If analytics are added in future, their cookies will be used only with your agreement.</p>

        <h2 id="keep">7. How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Course registrations:</strong> while you are studying with us and for up to three years after your last course, so that we can tell you about the next stage. After that, or sooner if you ask, we delete it.</li>
          <li><strong>News:</strong> until you unsubscribe. When you unsubscribe, you are removed from the email list straight away and we delete your details from the student register within 30 days unless you are still on a course.</li>
          <li><strong>Messages to us:</strong> up to two years, then deleted.</li>
          <li><strong>Technical logs</strong> kept by the web host: for the host’s own short retention period.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We may keep a minimal record (such as your email address and the date you withdrew consent) where the law requires it, or to make sure we do not email you again.</p>

        <h2 id="security">8. How we protect it</h2>
        <p>Access to the student register and the email service is limited to the people who run the courses, through accounts protected with two-step sign-in. Data is sent over encrypted connections. If a breach ever affects your personal information, we will tell you without delay, in plain language: what happened, what it may mean for you, what we are doing about it, and whom to contact. We will also inform the Data Protection Board of India as the law requires.</p>

        <h2 id="rights">9. Your rights</h2>
        <p>You can ask us:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>for a summary of the personal information we hold about you and how it is used;</li>
          <li>to correct, complete or update it;</li>
          <li>to delete it;</li>
          <li>to stop using it, by withdrawing your consent;</li>
          <li>to deal with a person you nominate, who can act for you if you die or are unable to.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> from the email address you registered with, or tell us how we can confirm it is you. We will reply within 30 days. There is no charge.</p>

        <h2 id="grievance">10. Questions and complaints</h2>
        <p>Please write first to {legal.grievanceOfficer}, at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> or {legal.address}. We will acknowledge your complaint and try to resolve it within 30 days. If you are not satisfied with our answer, you can complain to the <strong>Data Protection Board of India</strong>.</p>

        <h2 id="children">11. Children</h2>
        <p>Our courses are for adults. Please do not register if you are under 18. If we learn that someone under 18 has registered without a parent’s or guardian’s consent, we will delete their information.</p>

        <h2 id="changes">12. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>When we change this policy we will update the date at the top of the page. If a change affects how we use the information you have already given us, we will tell you by email and, where needed, ask for your consent again.</p>

        <p class="links"><a href={u('/terms')}>Terms of use</a> · <a href={u('/contact')}>Contact</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-text h2 { font-size: clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 26px); margin: 1.6em 0 .5em; }
  .summary { font-size: 18px; border-left: 2px solid var(--gold); padding-left: 16px; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 0 0 1.1em; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 16px; min-width: 560px; }
  th, td { text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: 12px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  thead th { font: 500 13px/1.3 var(--font-ui); letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold-text); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gold-line); }
  tbody th { font-weight: 600; width: 22%; }
  .links { margin-top: 2em; }
</style>
